Module container identity is keyed on the consumer's import-alias spelling,
not the resolved module: `a/pump` emits `koru_a.koru_pump` while the decl's
own `b/pump:Payload` (same file, other alias) is written `koru_b.koru_pump
.Payload` in the ?-optional-arm noop and Handlers signatures — a dangling
`use of undeclared identifier 'koru_b'`. Surfaced by koru-libs/metal drift.k
(`libs/metal` vs `koru/metal:KeyData`). Canonicalize emitted container names
on module identity; fix in the emitter, not the test.
